{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1335640-help-need-characters-and-behemoths","id":1335640,"title":"Help. Need characters and Behemoths","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-09-13T18:30:55-07:00","id":1335640,"title":"Help. Need characters and Behemoths","content":"Please share descriptions of celestial exalted you have played, played with, you have thought of etc. Mostly just looking for a name, description, motivation and how you think they would go about fulfilling it. I am happy to take more than that if you have it.<br /> <br /> Additionally if you can share behemoths you have found or written. Any and all fan primordial behemoths you can share or link to me.<br /> Thank you in advance.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1166-korekore","name":"korekore","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1166_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"141"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-13T18:59:30-07:00","id":1335642,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>korekore</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1335640-help-need-characters-and-behemoths#post1335640\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Please share descriptions of celestial exalted you have played, played with, you have thought of etc. Mostly just looking for a name, description, motivation and how you think they would go about fulfilling it. I am happy to take more than that if you have it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Knight Raiton is an Eclipse Caste Solar. He wears a cloak of ration feathers joined together with moonsilver wire over dark silk enchanted to turn aside blades. Knight Raiton wants to bring about safety and security in Nexus, such that a person could lie down and sleep in a gutter without fear. By day he masquerades as Guild factor Carter Brus, so as to undermine the absolute power wielded by the Council of Entities (and maybe work toward reforming the Guild).<br /> <br /> Spider is a Twilight Caste Solar, a tall lean man with yellow eyes. His eyebrows are pierced, dotted with six amber studs. He is a man of many hats, a clothier and a scavenger-lord, a sorcerer and a researcher. He finds no value in half-measures, and loves nothing greater than knowledge. Great Forks is his home, and at present his primary desires are to seek out knowledge and make trouble for those who only see power as a tool with which to oppress others.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-13T20:14:56-07:00","id":1335650,"title":"","content":"<i>Epitome</i> is a Lore Supernal Zenith with the heart of a Twilight. He believes he knows it all, is overconfident in all scholarly endeavors, and tends to give himself the credit for any successes his Circle achieves even when it is obvious to everyone else that he is full of it. He is over a hundred years old but looks like a vigorous 60 years old man. He sports a traditional wise man's long white beard, and he wears the most opulent scholarly attire he can get his hands on. A past incarnation left him a message warning him that Creation would need lost knowledge to keep the Wyld from devouring it, so he has devoted his life to studying First Age ruins and relics in hopes of learning how to best protect Creation from the Wyld.<br /> <br /> <i>Lonan</i> is an Archery Supernal Dawn who pretends to be a vengeful god of the North called Storm Sunder. His Artifact Bow, First Snow, contains the soul of a mystical owl with the same name. This owl is everything Lonan pretends to be, but it has died and now lives through those who wield its Artifact. The bow causes Lonan to receive the prayers directed at Storm Sunder, desperate prayers begging for vengeance and filled with despair. This in turn is slowly molding Lonan's personality into what people believe he is, a cold and vengeful god. Despite pretending to be a Northern god, anyone canny enough to see through Lonan's disguise would see him sneeze under his hood, as the man is actually really bad at dealing with the cold.<br /> <br /> <i>What Was Sown</i> is a Melee Supernal Dawn who travels the land as a wandering avenger, with no higher purpose than finding the next despicable foe to take down. A pair of artifact short swords grants him wings which are core to his acrobatic fighting style. Sown believes that no price is too high to pay to achieve justice. Embodying this belief is his cursed Reaper Daiklave called Rule Breaker. This artifact katana brings his powers to a completely different level, but each swing pokes at the Great Curse slumbering within him, bringing with it the risk that Sown will go overboard and end up destroying the very things he means to protect. For this reason, he only uses this weapon when he has no other choice or when he is swept away by strong emotions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25285,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25285-epitome","user":"Epitome","date":". 09-13-2019, 11:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25285-epitome","name":"Epitome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25285_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-13T23:20:59-07:00","id":1335670,"title":"","content":"Here's a Behemoth I made for one of my games :<br /> <br /> <b>name : </b>Akharenos, the Crystal that Binds<br /> <b>what is it </b>: semi-sentient Giant Crystal Golem that seeks to encase everything in crystal, drawn most strongly to sorcerous workings that reshape the land.<br /> <b>mechanics :</b><br /> -Charm that crystalizes the ground around the golem in a large area, rooting targets that are hit by the effect in place. Repeated use of the Charm applies an increasing penalty that culminates with the victim being encased in Crystal, knocking them out and causing death by asphyxiation if left alone. The crystallization of the area is permanent, leaving wastelands of jagged crystal formations in the behemoth's wake.<br /> -Charm that spreads clouds of sharp crystal shards in the air, creating an environmental hazard and giving a penalty to characters who try to avoid the first Charm by flying<br /> -The chunks that fall off the behemoth take on a life of their own. For every few health levels of damage the behemoth takes, smaller golems spawn.<br /> -The smaller golems spawn at short range from the behemoth. If unimpeded, they will immediately move back to the behemoth and use a misc action to merge with it, disappearing but healing the health levels that spawned them","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25285,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25285-epitome","user":"Epitome","date":". 09-14-2019, 09:56 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25285-epitome","name":"Epitome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25285_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-14T00:54:25-07:00","id":1335682,"title":"","content":"This is a behemoth that my players unleashed by... well, not working together, I guess is the easiest explanation. One Solar found this behemoth trapped under a manse, didn't tell the others, they later blew the manse up and so the behemoth escaped. It's ramped around for a while, but not near the PCs. The new ST said he might run it using the lava-behemoth from Hundred Devils, but he hasn't yet.<br /> <br /> <u><i>Asheedar, Author of Ten Thousand Tragedies. </i></u><br /> Asheedar has 8 clawed arms, 2 legs, and 3 heads: a tusked human, snake, tiger. It's about a mile tall. Its skin is dark blue, but when submerged in lava it turns gold and becomes soft. In fact, his powers are generally weakened when he's heated to a high degree, making a lava-prison the best way to bind him.<br /> All books and writing within 3 miles slowly twist into sentences that will cause division and strife for those who read them.<br /> Everyone in 7 miles can understand other languages, but badly, causing mistrust.<br /> Even the land near it distorts to form words of rock and wood that cause witnesses to go mad.<br /> For those who get close, its durrounded by floating, maddening script. All who can read Old Realm are attacked by a 16 dice social influence attempt to instill a Minor Derangement of Paranoia. As it's just recently escaped, Asheedar is revelling in destruction and carnage, though he also seeks to find ways to communicate with its father, He Who Bleeds the Unknown Word. If anyone is able to convince him to talk to a human, they will find he knows many secrets. But Asheedar lies and twists the truth, as he enjoys the chaos caused by misunderstandings and partial information.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}